5, \"task\": \"External Network Context Validation (IP Address)\", \"action\": \"Extract external IP addresses from the decoded 'scriptblock', 'get_recent_events', and 'get_recent_similar_alerts' results, then invoke 'check_ip_reputation' (AbuseIPDB) for each identified IP. This is only if they exist in the script or correlated data. If not, skip this step.\", \"tool_integration\": \"check_ip_reputation\", \"logic\": \"IP reputation is used as contextual enrichment only. Regardless of AbuseIPDB score, the presence of hard-coded external IP communication within scripts exhibiting reverse shell, command-and-control, or interactive execution behavior should be treated as malicious by behavior. Reputation data is used to strengthen confidence, identify infrastructure reuse, and support campaign correlation\\u00e2\\u20ac\\u201dnot to downgrade severity.\"}, {\"step_id\": 6, \"task\": \"Final Triage Classification\", \"action\": \"Assign triage priority (LP or HP) by correlating process legitimacy, script behavior, execution context, VirusTotal results, and network indicators, factoring in 'file_path' existence when available.\", \"logic\": \"Classification rules:\\n\\n1. **Low Priority (LP)** if:\\n   - The 'file_path' (if exists) is a known authorized application or system directory.\\n   - AND process lineage correlates to legitimate software activity (VirusTotal < 5 detections).\\n   - AND script logic aligns with a documented functional or administrative requirement.\\n   - AND no command-and-control, reverse shell, or interactive remote execution behavior is observed.\\n\\n2. **High Priority (HP)** if:\\n   - The script exhibits command-and-control, reverse shell, beaconing, or interactive execution behavior, regardless of IP reputation.\\n   - OR VirusTotal reports 5 or more detections for the initiating process.\\n   - OR the alert lacks a 'file_path' while performing suspicious discovery, persistence, or network-based execution (potential fileless execution).\\n   - OR 'file_path' exists but is highly suspicious (e.g., \\\\Users\\\\Public\\\\, \\\\Temp\\\\).\\n   - OR the same external IP is observed across multiple recent events or similar alerts, indicating possible infrastructure reuse.\\n   - OR the script is heavily obfuscated and lacks identifiable authorized application paths.\"}, {\"step_id\": 7, \"task\": \"Generate Investigation Summary\", \"action\": \"Construct a concise Description field including: 1) Script intent, 2) File Path existence/legitimacy (mentioning if the field was missing), 3) VT and AbuseIPDB results, if they exist, and 4) Final reasoning.\", \"logic\": \"Ensures the summary explicitly clarifies whether the triage was based on a physical file path or script behavior alone.\"}]}\nAlert: {\"alert_id\": \"SOC-9826\", \"alert_name\": \"Suspicious PowerShell Script Execution\", \"start_time\": \"2026-01-27T01:36:54.000Z\", \"source_ip\": \"10.5.14.92\", \"endpoint\": \"HR-SRV-02\", \"user\": \"k.tamm\", \"user_id\": \"S-1-5-21-88990011-22334455-66778899-1034\", \"description\": \"A suspicious PowerShell script was executed on the host.\", \"evidence\": {\"scriptblock\": \"Copy-Item 'C:\\\\Users\\\\*\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Google\\\\Chrome\\\\User Data\\\\Default\\\\Login Data' -Destination C:\\\\ProgramData\\\\chrome_cache.db -Force; Copy-Item 'C:\\\\Users\\\\*\\\\AppData\\\\Roaming\\\\Mozilla\\\\Firefox\\\\Profiles\\\\*.default-release\\\\logins.json' -Destination C:\\\\ProgramData\\\\ff_cache.json -Force\", \"os\": \"Windows Server 2019 Standard\"}}"
